card.statement:
Let $M$ be a simple Gelfand-Tsetlin module. Then the following hold.

- [(i)] For every $\lambda \in \Supp M$, every eigenvalue of $A_{\lambda}$ has multiplicity
at most $2$.

- [(ii)] If $(\mu_{i})_{i\in J}$ is a connected chain of the set of distinct eigenvalues of $A_{\lambda}=A\mid_{M_{\lambda}}$, then

- [(a)] if the chain $(\mu_{i})_{i\in J}$ is generic then all eigenvalues of $A_{\lambda}$ are distinct;

- [(b)] if the chain $(\mu_{i})_{i\in J}$ is degenerate then the chain can be chosen so that $\mu_1=-\frac{r}{2}$, and if the multiplicity of $\mu_i$ equals $1$
then the multiplicity of $\mu_{i+1}$ is also $1$;

- [(c)] if the chain $(\mu_{i})_{i\in J}$ is critical then the chain can be chosen so that $\mu_1+1=\mu_2$, the multiplicity of $\mu_1$ is $1$, and if the multiplicity of $\mu_i$ equals $1$ for $i>1$, then the multiplicity of $\mu_{i+1}$ also equals $1$;

- [(d)] if the chain $(\mu_{i})_{i\in J}$ is singular but not degenerate or critical, then all eigenvalues of $A_{\lambda}$ are distinct.
